{
 "title": "El operador ?",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "Los `match` anidados se complican rápido. El **operador `?`** pasa un error hacia arriba: si la función llamada devolvió `Ok(v)`, `?` extrae el valor `v`; si devolvió `Err(e)`, la función en la que estás se detiene **de inmediato** y devuelve ese mismo error a quien la llamó."
  },
  {
   "t": "code",
   "code": [
    "fn step_one() -> Result[i32, str]:",
    "    return Ok(10)",
    "",
    "fn step_two(x: i32) -> Result[i32, str]:",
    "    if x > 5:",
    "        return Ok(x * 2)",
    "    return Err(\"x is too small\")",
    "",
    "fn workflow() -> Result[i32, str]:",
    "    val1 = step_one()?",
    "    val2 = step_two(val1)?",
    "    return Ok(val2 + 5)",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    match workflow():",
    "        Ok(v):",
    "            print(\"succeeded:\", v)",
    "        Err(msg):",
    "            print(\"failed:\", msg)"
   ],
   "run": true,
   "output": [
    "succeeded: 25"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "Regla: `?` se usa solo en expresiones completas (`x = f()?`, `return f()?`, `f()?`). No se puede usar en subexpresiones como `g(f()?)` o `x += f()?`."
  },
  {
   "t": "exercise",
   "id": "c08-l04-x1",
   "prompt": "Escribe `parse_and_double(a: i32) -> Result[i32, str]`: valida con `check(a)?` (`Err(\"negative\")` si es negativo) y luego devuelve `Ok(a * 2)`. Pruébala con 21 y -4.",
   "starter": [
    "fn check(a: i32) -> Result[i32, str]:",
    "    if a < 0:",
    "        return Err(\"negative\")",
    "    return Ok(a)",
    "",
    "fn parse_and_double(a: i32) -> Result[i32, str]:",
    "    return Ok(0)",
    "",
    "fn show(a: i32):",
    "    match parse_and_double(a):",
    "        Ok(v):",
    "            print(\"ok\", v)",
    "        Err(m):",
    "            print(\"error:\", m)",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    show(21)",
    "    show(-4)"
   ],
   "solution": [
    "fn check(a: i32) -> Result[i32, str]:",
    "    if a < 0:",
    "        return Err(\"negative\")",
    "    return Ok(a)",
    "",
    "fn parse_and_double(a: i32) -> Result[i32, str]:",
    "    v = check(a)?",
    "    return Ok(v * 2)",
    "",
    "fn show(a: i32):",
    "    match parse_and_double(a):",
    "        Ok(v):",
    "            print(\"ok\", v)",
    "        Err(m):",
    "            print(\"error:\", m)",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    show(21)",
    "    show(-4)"
   ],
   "hint": "Escribe `v = check(a)?` y luego devuelve `Ok(v * 2)`.",
   "expected": [
    "ok 42",
    "error: negative"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "quiz",
   "id": "c08-l04-q1",
   "q": "En `x = f()?`, ¿qué ocurre si `f()` devuelve `Err`?",
   "options": [
    "`x` pasa a ser 0",
    "La función actual devuelve de inmediato el mismo error",
    "El programa se cae"
   ],
   "answer": 1,
   "why": "`?` retorna antes de tiempo y pasa el error hacia arriba."
  }
 ]
}
